WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.080
A new actor is taking the blade, but some
people are still thinking of the guy who started

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:05.580
it all.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.980
Marvel Studios announced that Mahershala Ali
will lead a reboot of Blade, starring as the

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:15.989
vampire-hunter and skilled swordsman Eric
Brooks, a half-vampire who, in the comics,

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:17.920
is on a quest to avenge his mother's death.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.220
People went wild at the announcement.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.980
An Academy Award-winning actor breathing new
life into the Blade property?

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.080
Sounds killer!

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.560
But wait, what about the man Ali is taking
over for in the Blade reboot?

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.860
"What's so funny, bright eyes?"

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.440
"I'm expecting company!"

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.960
Now that Ali is firmly aboard the in-development
movie, it appears that original Blade actor

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.100
Wesley Snipes is sunsetting his iconic role
for good.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.260
However, Snipes' fans are holding out hope
that Marvel can make room for him in the Blade

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.680
reboot — or else there might be hell to
pay.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.320
Taking to Twitter, one fan suggested that
Marvel should tap Snipes for the role of Abraham

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.850
Whistler – Blade's mentor and weaponsmith
whom Kris Kristofferson portrayed in the original

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.380
Blade trilogy — as a way to honor the actor.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.240
They tweeted:

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.680
"Let's start the movement right here, right
now, for @MarvelStudios to cast @wesleysnipes

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.570
as Whistler in the reboot of #BladeMCU.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:19.850
The entire current run of comic-book movies
owes everything to the 1st Blade movie, so

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:23.180
a little honouring of the legacy he left isn't
too much to ask."

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:28.070
Another said that no matter how great Ali
is in the role, Snipes will forever be the

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.400
actor associated with Blade.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.060
They tweeted:

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.940
"Wesley Snipes still is the baddest Blade
we'll ever see in this lifetime.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.680
Even though the role has been given to [Mahershala
Ali] in a reboot, special respect to this

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.180
man!!!"

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.020
Elsewhere, fans said that the Blade reboot,
quote, "won't go over well" without Snipes

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:48.810
involved, that Snipes, quote, "deserves" a
cameo or a supporting role in the movie, and

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.729
that Marvel can go ahead and cancel the film
ahead of time because they don't want it if

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:53.980
Snipes isn't starring.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.140
User @DavidWDougan argued:

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:01.520
"I think a #Blade reboot is long overdue,
but Mahershala Ali has his work cut out if

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.420
he wants to be cooler as the character than
Wesley Snipes was."

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.870
Meanwhile, @DakotaMiller said:

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:12.400
"I'm the biggest Blade fan ever &amp; super stoked
about Marvel announcing the reboot, but if

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.280
Wesley Snipes isn't at least in a cameo I'm
gonna riot."

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:22.200
On the flip side, Twitter user @Guavah_Go
wrote that Blade fans should be more open-minded

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:27.200
about Ali's casting, stop focusing so much
on the past, and have faith in how Ali will

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.340
approach the new iteration of the character.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.420
Their tweet reads:

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:35.129
"We can appreciate Wesley Snipes as Blade
and also be excited for the reboot.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:36.360
You CAN have both.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:38.780
Wesley Snipes was excellent as #Blade.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:44.160
Ali won't be playing that same version, obviously,
hopefully he brings his own style &amp; dynamic

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:44.940
to the role."

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:50.000
These reactions to Ali's casting as Blade
in the upcoming reboot movie may seem dramatic,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.420
but they're not at all surprising.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.950
Snipes has long made it clear that he's ready
to return to the role he originated with 1998's

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.380
Blade, a film that changed superhero movies
forever.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:04.720
In December of 2018, the 56-year-old actor
took to Twitter to affirm that his teeth are,

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:08.950
quote, "still sharp" for a Blade reboot, and
that it's simply up to Marvel if they'd like

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.519
to bring him back on board.

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:15.709
A few months later, Snipes sat down with Vice
and opened up about the possibility of a fourth

00:03:15.709 --> 00:03:18.879
Blade movie to follow after Blade: Trinity,
saying

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:23.000
"There are a lot of conversations going around
right now and we're very blessed to have the

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.700
enthusiasm and interest in something coming
from that world again.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:31.920
All the main execs [at Marvel] and my team,
we've been discussing for the past two years.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.529
Everyone's enthusiastic about it, everybody
gets it.

00:03:34.529 --> 00:03:38.010
But they got a business to run and they gotta
square the things that they gotta figure out

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:39.709
before they can get to it, I guess."

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:44.819
Fast forward to summer 2019, and it was reported
that Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:48.799
was "fighting" for a new Blade movie — with
Snipes attached in the lead role.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:49.920
So, what happened?

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.900
Well, Mahershala Ali happened.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:56.440
The Green Book and Moonlight actor rang up
Marvel Studios and essentially pitched himself

00:03:56.449 --> 00:04:00.769
as the new Blade, and there was no denying
the powerhouse talent his wish.

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:01.600
As Feige put it:

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.040
"When Mahershala calls, you answer."

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.740
“That must've hurt."

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.779
There's no telling whether the studio will
be receptive if Snipes says point-blank that

00:04:10.779 --> 00:04:15.339
he wants a part in the Blade reboot, but considering
that the star essentially paved the way for

00:04:15.339 --> 00:04:19.621
all superhero actors who came after him and
that his fans are gunning hard for him to

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.840
join the new movie, Marvel would be smart
to not screen his call.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:27.240
"Some m-----------s are always tryin to ice skate uphill."

